nts): needs 123+456+789 in same suit \u2014 not feasible here.\n  - **Two Terminal Chows** (1 point): if you form W789 and another chow, but not applicable.\n  - **Short Straight** (2 points): e.g., W789 and W567 \u2192 not possible.\n\nBut your meld [B2,B3,B4] is fixed \u2014 so you cannot achieve Full Flush or Upper Tiles due to mixed suits.\n\nSimilarly, T6 and T8 prevent All Simples unless paired.\n\nBetter direction: pursue **Mixed Shifted Pungs/Chows**, but you lack pungs.\n\nAlternatively, consider **All Pungs** (6 points), but you have only one chow and rest are pairs/singles.\n\nCurrent shape: many pairs: W8, W9, T6, T8 are pairs; W7, B3, J2 singletons.\n\nIf you keep pairing, could go for **Seven Pairs** (24 points)!\n\nCheck: current concealed hand: need to know exact composition.\n\nAssume the hand is: W7, W8, W8, W9, W9, T6, T6, T8, T8, B3, J2 \u2014 11 tiles.\n\nStill missing two.\n\nPerhaps the hand list is incomplete, or we must infer.\n\nAnother possibility: the \u201chand tiles\u201d list uses colon notation meaning \u201ccount\u201d, but actual hand has duplicates accounted.\n\nBut 11 tiles only.\n\nUnless the meld [B2,B3,B4] is counted separately, and hand is 11, meaning you have 11 concealed + 3 exposed = 14 \u2192 but you should have 13 concealed before draw.\n\nThis is confusing.\n\nAlternative: perhaps after Chi, you had 12, then drew and discarded four times \u2014 impossible in standard order.\n\nBest way: **focus on patterns and choices.**\n\nYou are to discard one of: J2, T8, W8, W7, B3, T6, W9\n\nThese are all in hand.\n\nThe fact that you can discard W7, W8, W9 means you have at least one each.\n\nSimilarly, T6 and T8 are in hand.\n\nJ2 and B3 also.\n\nNow, evaluate:\n\n- **W suit (Characters)**: W7, W8\u00d72, W9\u00d72 \u2192 very strong group. Together they form potential for:\n  - A pung of W8 or W9 if you draw another\n  - Part of a terminal flush\n  - But your meld [B2,B3,B4] locks in a lower bamboo chow, breaking pure hands.\n\n-